If I remember correctly, the MAZE-type special levels don't usually keep the
room numbers, except unless specially told for each room, or if the room
is a special room, such as a shop or a graveyard.

Randomly generated dungeons in the DoD, or LEVEL-type special levels
do keep the room numbers.

eg. dat/knox.des: (which is a MAZE-type level)
#   arrival chamber; needs to be a real room to control migrating monsters,
#   and `unfilled' is a kludge to force an ordinary room to remain a room
REGION:(06,15,09,16),unlit,"ordinary",unfilled

So, I'd think you'll have to do a flood-fill to find all connected
areas if not in a room.

